  ($qb$S06C08Q04$qb$, $qb$S06$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$MM+E$qb$, $qb$The frequency of recognition relative to the frequency of criticism or correction in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Positive — recognition significantly outweighs criticism; employees feel more appreciated than scrutinised$qb$, $qb$Balanced — recognition and correction are roughly equal$qb$, $qb$Correction-heavy — employees hear more about what is wrong than what is right$qb$, $qb$Criticism-dominant — the dominant management communication mode is finding fault, not recognising achievement$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
