  ($qb$S06C08Q09$qb$, $qb$S06$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Recognition for innovation, learning, and experimentation (not just results) in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Active — employees are recognised for trying, learning, and innovating regardless of the outcome$qb$, $qb$Occasional — innovative behaviour is sometimes recognised when it is highly visible$qb$, $qb$Rare — recognition is almost exclusively for results; process and learning are not rewarded$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — only results are recognised; experimentation that fails is not rewarded$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S06C08Q10$qb$, $qb$S06$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$Overall, the recognition and reward experience in your organisation reinforces the performance culture:$qb$, $qb$Strongly — recognition and reward make high performance feel visibly valued$qb$, $qb$Moderately — recognition supports performance culture but with notable gaps$qb$, $qb$Weakly — recognition and reward do not significantly reinforce the performance culture$qb$, $qb$Not at all — the disconnect between performance and recognition actively undermines the performance culture$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S06C09Q01$qb$, $qb$S06$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Performance management practices in your organisation have adapted effectively to remote or hybrid working:$qb$, $qb$Yes — performance management has been redesigned to work effectively regardless of physical location$qb$, $qb$Not applicable — the organisation is fully on-site and this category does not apply$qb$, $qb$Minimally — on-site performance management practices have been transposed to remote without adaptation$qb$, $qb$No adaptation — performance management in remote or hybrid settings is significantly weaker$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S06C09Q02$qb$, $qb$S06$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Managers in your organisation can effectively assess the performance of remote employees:$qb$, $qb$Yes — managers have the skills and tools to assess performance independent of physical observation$qb$, $qb$Not applicable — the organisation does not have remote or hybrid employees$qb$, $qb$Partially — remote employee performance is harder to assess and some managers default to presence bias$qb$, $qb$Poorly — remote employee assessment is significantly weaker than on-site$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S06C09Q03$qb$, $qb$S06$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$MM+E$qb$, $qb$Remote employees in your organisation feel their performance is fairly assessed compared to on-site employees:$qb$, $qb$Yes — remote employees feel equally and fairly assessed regardless of location$qb$, $qb$Not applicable — there are no remote employees in this organisation$qb$, $qb$Partially — remote employees perceive a systematic disadvantage in performance assessment$qb$, $qb$No — remote employees feel significantly disadvantaged in performance management$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
