  ($qb$S07C06Q05$qb$, $qb$S07$qb$, $qb$C06$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Internal knowledge-sharing platforms (intranets, wikis, Confluence, SharePoint) in your organisation are:$qb$, $qb$Well-maintained and actively used — employees regularly contribute and access knowledge$qb$, $qb$Available but underused — platforms exist but adoption is low$qb$, $qb$Outdated — platforms exist but content is stale and not trusted$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — no knowledge management platform is in use$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S07C06Q06$qb$, $qb$S07$qb$, $qb$C06$qb$, $qb$MM+E$qb$, $qb$Cross-departmental knowledge sharing in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Structured — regular cross-functional sessions, shared repositories, and communities of practice exist$qb$, $qb$Occasional — some cross-functional learning happens but it is not structured$qb$, $qb$Rare — knowledge stays within departments and is not shared across functions$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — silos prevent any meaningful knowledge exchange$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S07C06Q07$qb$, $qb$S07$qb$, $qb$C06$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The organisation's intellectual property (proprietary methods, frameworks, client insights) is:$qb$, $qb$Protected and systematically developed — IP is captured, maintained, and used as a competitive asset$qb$, $qb$Partially captured — some IP is documented but much remains informal$qb$, $qb$Loosely managed — IP exists but is not consistently documented or protected$qb$, $qb$Not managed — the organisation does not treat its knowledge as a strategic asset$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
