  ($qb$S08C04Q04$qb$, $qb$S08$qb$, $qb$C04$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$When a key employee gives notice in your organisation, the operational impact is:$qb$, $qb$Manageable — succession plans and knowledge transfer processes minimise disruption$qb$, $qb$Noticeable but recoverable — some disruption occurs but is managed within weeks$qb$, $qb$Significant — the departure creates operational problems that take months to resolve$qb$, $qb$Severe — key departures regularly create crises that take many months to recover from$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S08C04Q05$qb$, $qb$S08$qb$, $qb$C04$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Talent risk (the risk of losing critical people) is on your organisation's risk register:$qb$, $qb$Yes — talent risk is formally assessed, rated, and reported to the board$qb$, $qb$Partially — talent risk is discussed at senior level but not formally on the risk register$qb$, $qb$Informally — talent risk is acknowledged but not formally managed$qb$, $qb$No — talent is not treated as an organisational risk$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S08C04Q06$qb$, $qb$S08$qb$, $qb$C04$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Diversity in the succession pipeline (women, underrepresented groups ready for senior roles) in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Actively managed — diverse succession candidates are identified and specifically developed$qb$, $qb$Acknowledged — diversity in succession is a stated goal but progress is slow$qb$, $qb$Aspirational — diversity in succession is mentioned but not structurally addressed$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — succession planning does not consider diversity$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S08C04Q07$qb$, $qb$S08$qb$, $qb$C04$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The time to fill a critical role vacancy in your organisation (through internal succession or external hiring) is:$qb$, $qb$Short (under 60 days) — strong succession and rapid external search capability minimise vacancy periods$qb$, $qb$Moderate (60–120 days) — vacancies are filled within a reasonable timeframe$qb$, $qb$Long (120–180 days) — critical role vacancies persist for extended periods$qb$, $qb$Very long (over 180 days) — critical role vacancies are a recurring operational crisis$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S08C04Q08$qb$, $qb$S08$qb$, $qb$C04$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Buy vs build decisions for critical talent (whether to develop internally or hire externally) in your organisation are:$qb$, $qb$Made strategically — the organisation has a clear philosophy and applies it consistently$qb$, $qb$Made on a case-by-case basis with some strategic thinking$qb$, $qb$Made reactively — the immediate pressure of a vacancy drives the decision$qb$, $qb$Not made deliberately — the default is always external hiring regardless of internal potential$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S08C04Q09$qb$, $qb$S08$qb$, $qb$C04$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The board's engagement with talent risk and succession in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Active — the board reviews succession for C-suite roles and monitors talent risk$qb$, $qb$Periodic — the board sees succession data annually or when prompted$qb$, $qb$Minimal — the board receives limited talent risk information$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — the board does not engage with talent risk or succession$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S08C04Q10$qb$, $qb$S08$qb$, $qb$C04$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Overall talent risk exposure in your organisation (vulnerability to losing key people) is:$qb$, $qb$Low — the organisation is well-protected against talent loss through succession and retention$qb$, $qb$Moderate — some vulnerability exists but critical areas are covered$qb$, $qb$High — several critical areas are exposed to significant talent risk$qb$, $qb$Very high — the organisation is highly vulnerable to talent loss in multiple critical areas$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S08C05Q01$qb$, $qb$S08$qb$, $qb$C05$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Your organisation's reputation as an employer (on Glassdoor, LinkedIn, word of mouth) is:$qb$, $qb$Positive and managed — reviews are monitored, responded to, and the organisation actively builds its employer brand$qb$, $qb$Neutral — employer brand is not particularly strong or weak$qb$, $qb$Mixed — positive and negative reviews exist and the negatives are not being systematically addressed$qb$, $qb$Negative — employer brand problems are deterring quality candidates and contributing to attrition$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
