  ($qb$S08C05Q04$qb$, $qb$S08$qb$, $qb$C05$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The experience employees describe to outsiders when asked what it is like to work at your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Predominantly positive — most employees are genuine advocates$qb$, $qb$Mixed — some employees are positive; others are openly critical$qb$, $qb$Predominantly neutral or negative — most employees are not advocates$qb$, $qb$Actively negative — the internal employer brand is so poor that employees warn others away$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S08C05Q05$qb$, $qb$S08$qb$, $qb$C05$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The gap between the employer brand presented externally (EVP, careers page) and the lived internal experience is:$qb$, $qb$Minimal — what is promised is largely what is delivered$qb$, $qb$Small — some gaps exist but they are not large enough to cause significant disappointment$qb$, $qb$Significant — new hires regularly find the reality does not match the promise$qb$, $qb$Large — employer brand misrepresentation is a primary driver of early attrition$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
