  ($qb$S09C08Q02$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Accountability for results in the sales team is:$qb$, $qb$Clear and consistently applied — performance is owned at every level$qb$, $qb$Generally present — accountability exists but is not always consistently applied$qb$, $qb$Inconsistent — some salespeople are held accountable; others are not$qb$, $qb$Very weak — accountability is inconsistent and underperformance is frequently not addressed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C08Q03$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$Collaboration between salespeople (sharing leads, best practices, support) is:$qb$, $qb$A genuine cultural norm — the team helps each other win$qb$, $qb$Happens among some — some collaboration exists but it is not universal$qb$, $qb$Limited — the team is largely individualistic$qb$, $qb$Non-existent or competitive — salespeople guard information and compete destructively$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C08Q04$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Customer-centricity in the sales approach is:$qb$, $qb$Strong — the team genuinely sells to solve customer problems, not just to hit numbers$qb$, $qb$Generally present — customer needs are considered alongside commercial goals$qb$, $qb$Weak — the team is primarily focused on closing rather than on customer value$qb$, $qb$Very weak — the sales approach is transactional and pushes products regardless of customer fit$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C08Q05$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$Ethical selling practices (no mis-selling, no pressure tactics, accurate promises) are:$qb$, $qb$A strong cultural norm — ethics in selling is explicitly valued and any breach is addressed$qb$, $qb$Generally maintained — ethical issues are rare$qb$, $qb$Inconsistently maintained — some salespeople make promises the business cannot keep$qb$, $qb$Weak — mis-selling, exaggeration, or pressure tactics are known to occur$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C08Q06$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$Celebration and recognition of sales achievement is:$qb$, $qb$Genuine and motivating — wins are celebrated in meaningful and timely ways$qb$, $qb$Present — wins are recognised but the impact of recognition could be stronger$qb$, $qb$Inconsistent — some wins are recognised; others go unacknowledged$qb$, $qb$Very limited — little genuine celebration of achievement occurs$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C08Q07$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Resilience and response to rejection or losing deals in your organisation's sales team is:$qb$, $qb$Strong — the team learns from losses and bounces back quickly$qb$, $qb$Generally adequate — resilience is present in most of the team$qb$, $qb$Variable — some salespeople struggle significantly with rejection$qb$, $qb$Weak — morale is fragile and setbacks have an outsized negative effect on team motivation$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C08Q08$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The relationship between the sales team and the delivery/operations team is:$qb$, $qb$Collaborative — sales and delivery work closely together to manage customer expectations$qb$, $qb$Generally functional — some friction exists but it is managed$qb$, $qb$Tense — sales-delivery tension creates operational problems and customer dissatisfaction$qb$, $qb$Adversarial — conflict between sales and delivery is a persistent organisational problem$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C08Q09$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Transparency of pipeline and performance data within the sales team is:$qb$, $qb$High — pipeline, performance, and ranking are visible to all and drive healthy competition$qb$, $qb$Adequate — key data is shared without full transparency$qb$, $qb$Limited — data is shared on a need-to-know basis$qb$, $qb$Very limited — performance data is held by management and not shared with the team$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C08Q10$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$Overall, the sales culture and performance environment in your organisation:$qb$, $qb$Creates a genuine competitive advantage — the environment attracts and retains great salespeople$qb$, $qb$Is adequate — performance is maintained but the culture is not exceptional$qb$, $qb$Is a limiting factor — culture issues are constraining sales performance$qb$, $qb$Is a serious problem — the sales culture is damaging performance, ethics, or retention$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C09Q01$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Key account management in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Structured and relationship-deep — strategic accounts have dedicated managers and account plans$qb$, $qb$Adequate — key accounts receive attention but without formal account plans$qb$, $qb$Informal — key accounts are managed by the salesperson who won them without structured oversight$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — all customers are managed the same regardless of their strategic importance$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C09Q02$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The quality of relationships between your organisation and its most important customers is:$qb$, $qb$Strong — senior relationships exist at multiple levels and are proactively maintained$qb$, $qb$Generally good — relationships are professional and functional$qb$, $qb$Fragile — key relationships are concentrated in one or two individuals$qb$, $qb$Weak — customer relationships are transactional with limited depth or loyalty$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C09Q03$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Customer satisfaction measurement in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Regular and structured — NPS or CSAT data is collected, reported, and drives action$qb$, $qb$Periodic — customer satisfaction is measured but not as often or as deeply as needed$qb$, $qb$Occasional — satisfaction is measured when problems emerge$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — the organisation does not systematically measure customer satisfaction$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C09Q04$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$Response time and quality when customers raise concerns in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — issues are acknowledged quickly, resolved fairly, and followed up$qb$, $qb$Generally good — most complaints are handled adequately$qb$, $qb$Variable — response quality depends on the individual handling the issue$qb$, $qb$Poor — complaint handling is slow, inadequate, or damages the relationship$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C09Q05$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Customer success reviews (proactive meetings to assess satisfaction and expand opportunity) are:$qb$, $qb$Conducted regularly with all key accounts — generating expansion revenue and early warning of churn risk$qb$, $qb$Conducted for some accounts — the practice exists but is not universal$qb$, $qb$Done only when the customer initiates — the organisation is not proactive$qb$, $qb$Not done — the organisation does not conduct proactive customer success reviews$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C09Q06$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Escalation handling for major customer issues in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Structured — senior leadership is involved quickly in critical customer issues$qb$, $qb$Adequate — escalations are managed but not always with the speed or seniority required$qb$, $qb$Slow — escalations often take too long to reach the right level$qb$, $qb$Poor — major customer issues are not consistently escalated or resolved satisfactorily$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C09Q07$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Voice of Customer (structured customer feedback into product and service development) in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Systematic — customer feedback is captured, analysed, and influences decisions$qb$, $qb$Partially systematic — some structured customer feedback exists but is not comprehensive$qb$, $qb$Informal — customer feedback reaches the organisation through sales and support conversations$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — customer feedback is not systematically collected or used$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C09Q08$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The organisation's ability to recognise and act on early signs of customer dissatisfaction or churn risk is:$qb$, $qb$Strong — customer health monitoring identifies at-risk customers before they churn$qb$, $qb$Moderate — some at-risk signals are identified and acted on$qb$, $qb$Weak — churn is typically only known when the customer gives notice$qb$, $qb$Very weak — the organisation is consistently surprised by customer churn$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C09Q09$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$Customer data quality (completeness, accuracy, and currency of customer records) is:$qb$, $qb$High — customer data is clean, complete, and trusted$qb$, $qb$Generally adequate — data quality is acceptable with known gaps$qb$, $qb$Variable — customer data quality varies significantly across the customer base$qb$, $qb$Poor — customer data is incomplete, inaccurate, or fragmented across systems$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C09Q10$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Overall, the quality of customer relationship management in your organisation:$qb$, $qb$Creates loyal, expanding customer relationships that generate referrals and renewal$qb$, $qb$Maintains adequate customer relationships that are generally retained$qb$, $qb$Produces transactional relationships with limited depth or loyalty$qb$, $qb$Results in fragile customer relationships with high churn risk$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C10Q01$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Revenue forecasting accuracy in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$High — monthly and quarterly forecasts are within 5-10% of actuals consistently$qb$, $qb$Moderate — forecasts are directionally correct but precision is variable$qb$, $qb$Low — forecasts frequently miss actuals by more than 20%$qb$, $qb$Very low — forecasting is unreliable and creates significant business planning problems$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C10Q02$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$The forecasting process in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Bottom-up and validated — individual salesperson forecasts are reviewed against pipeline data$qb$, $qb$Partially bottom-up — individual input is gathered but not rigorously validated$qb$, $qb$Primarily top-down — targets are divided without genuine bottom-up pipeline validation$qb$, $qb$Finance-driven — revenue forecasts are financial models without genuine sales input$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C10Q03$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Revenue operations (alignment of sales, marketing, and customer success data and process) in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Mature — a RevOps function aligns all revenue-generating teams$qb$, $qb$Developing — some RevOps thinking is in place$qb$, $qb$Nascent — the concept is understood but not yet implemented$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — sales, marketing, and customer success operate independently$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C10Q04$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The linkage between sales pipeline and financial planning in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Tight — financial plans are based on validated sales pipeline data$qb$, $qb$Adequate — some connection exists between sales pipeline and financial planning$qb$, $qb$Weak — financial planning uses high-level assumptions without detailed pipeline grounding$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — financial planning and sales pipeline are disconnected$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C10Q05$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Deal-level risk assessment in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Structured — every forecast deal has a risk rating and mitigation plan$qb$, $qb$Partial — risk assessment happens for large deals but not systematically$qb$, $qb$Informal — experienced managers intuitively assess deal risk without a structured approach$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — deals are forecast as committed without risk assessment$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C10Q06$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The cadence of revenue review in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Weekly — pipeline and forecast are reviewed weekly at team and management level$qb$, $qb$Monthly — revenue performance is reviewed monthly$qb$, $qb$Quarterly — performance is reviewed at quarter end when it is too late to course-correct$qb$, $qb$Irregularly — revenue performance is reviewed when leadership requests it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C10Q07$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Early warning systems for revenue shortfalls in your organisation are:$qb$, $qb$In place — leading indicators signal risk weeks ahead of the period end$qb$, $qb$Partially in place — some early warning signals exist but are not consistently monitored$qb$, $qb$Weak — revenue risk is typically identified close to the period end$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — revenue shortfalls are discovered only at period end$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C10Q08$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$Sales performance reporting in your organisation provides:$qb$, $qb$Real-time actionable insight — dashboards enable immediate management decision-making$qb$, $qb$Adequate periodic reporting — regular reports are useful but not always timely$qb$, $qb$Lagging reporting — data arrives too late to drive timely management action$qb$, $qb$Minimal reporting — sales performance reporting is insufficient for effective management$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C10Q09$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The organisation's ability to model revenue scenarios (best case, worst case, base case) is:$qb$, $qb$Strong — scenario modelling is a standard planning tool used in strategic decisions$qb$, $qb$Adequate — some scenario thinking occurs at planning time$qb$, $qb$Limited — financial planning uses a single scenario without meaningful contingency analysis$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — scenario modelling is not a planning practice$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S09C10Q10$qb$, $qb$S09$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Overall, the quality of sales forecasting and revenue operations in your organisation:$qb$, $qb$Provides reliable visibility that enables proactive management of the business$qb$, $qb$Gives adequate directional insight with known limitations$qb$, $qb$Creates uncertainty that limits effective planning$qb$, $qb$Is a significant management handicap — unreliable revenue data impairs decision-making$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true);
