  ($qb$S10C01Q01$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the clarity and differentiation of brand identity is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — brand is clear, differentiated, and consistently expressed across all channels$qb$, $qb$Adequate — brand is defined but not always compelling or consistently applied$qb$, $qb$Weak — brand exists but is vague and not clearly differentiated$qb$, $qb$Very poor — brand is absent or incoherent, actively limiting growth$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C01Q02$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the value proposition is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — value proposition is precise, compelling, and understood by all stakeholders$qb$, $qb$Adequate — value proposition is defined but not always as compelling in competitive contexts$qb$, $qb$Weak — value proposition is generic and fails to differentiate from competitors$qb$, $qb$Very poor — value proposition does not exist or cannot be articulated by the team$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C01Q03$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the consistency of brand across all touchpoints is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — brand experience is identical regardless of channel, person, or touchpoint$qb$, $qb$Adequate — brand is generally consistent with occasional variation$qb$, $qb$Weak — brand varies significantly across touchpoints, undermining credibility$qb$, $qb$Very poor — brand is so inconsistent that stakeholders question whether it is the same organisation$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C01Q04$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the investment in brand building is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — brand is treated as a strategic business asset with sustained funding and measurement$qb$, $qb$Adequate — some brand investment is made but it is not a consistent strategic priority$qb$, $qb$Weak — brand investment is ad hoc and produces limited measurable brand value$qb$, $qb$Very poor — no meaningful brand investment is made$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C01Q05$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the employee understanding of the brand is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — all employees understand the brand and consistently deliver it in their interactions$qb$, $qb$Adequate — most employees understand the brand at a basic level$qb$, $qb$Weak — employees are unclear on what the brand stands for$qb$, $qb$Very poor — employees cannot articulate the brand$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C01Q06$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the measurement of brand health over time is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — brand metrics (awareness, perception, NPS) are tracked, reported, and drive decisions$qb$, $qb$Adequate — some brand measurement occurs but not with sufficient consistency$qb$, $qb$Weak — brand health is assessed only when a business need forces it$qb$, $qb$Very poor — brand health is not measured$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C01Q07$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the employer brand in the talent market is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — the employer brand actively attracts quality candidates and reduces attrition$qb$, $qb$Adequate — employer brand is adequate — neutral perception in the talent market$qb$, $qb$Weak — employer brand is weak and the organisation is not known as a strong employer$qb$, $qb$Very poor — employer brand is negative, deterring quality candidates$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C01Q08$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the quality and professionalism of visual and verbal brand identity is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — brand identity is professional, distinctive, and consistently reflects the quality of the organisation$qb$, $qb$Adequate — brand identity is professional if not particularly distinctive$qb$, $qb$Weak — brand identity is below standard and does not reflect the quality of the organisation$qb$, $qb$Very poor — brand identity is unprofessional and actively damaging credibility$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C01Q09$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the gap between brand promise and actual customer experience is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — the organisation consistently delivers on its brand promise — the gap is minimal$qb$, $qb$Adequate — small gaps exist between promise and delivery but are not systematically damaging$qb$, $qb$Weak — notable differences between promise and delivery are undermining brand trust$qb$, $qb$Very poor — brand promise and reality are so misaligned that it is actively damaging the organisation$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C01Q10$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the overall brand identity as a competitive asset is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — brand is a genuine competitive asset that attracts customers, talent, and partners$qb$, $qb$Adequate — brand is functional but not particularly differentiated$qb$, $qb$Weak — brand is underperforming — not creating the value it should$qb$, $qb$Very poor — brand is a liability — actively limiting the organisation's growth$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C02Q01$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C02$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the brand awareness among target customer segments is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — most target customers are aware of the organisation and what it does$qb$, $qb$Adequate — awareness is sufficient for current commercial performance$qb$, $qb$Weak — many target customers are not aware of the organisation$qb$, $qb$Very poor — brand awareness is a significant constraint on growth$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C02Q02$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C02$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the customer perception of quality and reliability is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — customers widely see the organisation as high-quality, trustworthy, and reliable$qb$, $qb$Adequate — customer perception is generally positive though not exceptional$qb$, $qb$Weak — customer perception is mixed — some positive, some neutral or negative$qb$, $qb$Very poor — customer perception of quality or reliability is damaging commercial performance$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C02Q03$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C02$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the Net Promoter Score or equivalent customer advocacy measure is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — NPS is strong (50+) — customers are active advocates$qb$, $qb$Adequate — NPS is good (30-50) — positive advocacy with room for improvement$qb$, $qb$Weak — NPS is moderate (10-30) — neutral customer sentiment dominates$qb$, $qb$Very poor — NPS is weak or not measured — customers are not advocates$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C02Q04$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C02$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the organisation's reputation in its industry or sector is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — the organisation is respected as a sector leader or expert$qb$, $qb$Adequate — reputation is good — positive without sector leadership$qb$, $qb$Weak — the organisation is not particularly well-known or regarded in its sector$qb$, $qb$Very poor — the organisation has a negative reputation in its sector$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C02Q05$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C02$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the management of customer reviews and ratings on public platforms is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — reviews are actively monitored, responded to, and predominantly positive$qb$, $qb$Adequate — reviews are broadly positive though not actively managed$qb$, $qb$Weak — reviews are mixed with no active management strategy$qb$, $qb$Very poor — negative reviews are damaging brand and sales$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C02Q06$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C02$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the word-of-mouth and referral from existing customers is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — customers actively refer the organisation to peers — referrals are a significant new business source$qb$, $qb$Adequate — some referrals are generated but it is not a primary channel$qb$, $qb$Weak — word-of-mouth does not meaningfully contribute to business development$qb$, $qb$Very poor — word-of-mouth is working against the organisation in some markets$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C02Q07$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C02$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the thought leadership and content output is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — the organisation is seen as a knowledge leader — content drives awareness and credibility$qb$, $qb$Adequate — some thought leadership content exists but without a systematic programme$qb$, $qb$Weak — occasional content is produced without a strategy$qb$, $qb$Very poor — the organisation produces no meaningful thought leadership$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C02Q08$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C02$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the media coverage and PR is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — the organisation regularly generates positive coverage in relevant channels$qb$, $qb$Adequate — the organisation responds to media opportunities but does not proactively seek coverage$qb$, $qb$Weak — the organisation rarely appears in relevant media$qb$, $qb$Very poor — media management is absent or coverage is predominantly negative$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C02Q09$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C02$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the customer feedback collection and analysis is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — multiple channels are actively used and customer perception data regularly influences decisions$qb$, $qb$Adequate — some channels exist but feedback collection is not systematic$qb$, $qb$Weak — feedback is collected occasionally without structured channels$qb$, $qb$Very poor — the organisation does not systematically collect customer perception data$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S10C02Q10$qb$, $qb$S10$qb$, $qb$C02$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$In your organisation, the overall market awareness and customer perception is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — positive perception is a commercial strength driving customer choice and loyalty$qb$, $qb$Adequate — perception is adequate and supports current business without being a differentiator$qb$, $qb$Weak — weak perception is constraining growth and requiring compensatory effort$qb$, $qb$Very poor — negative or low awareness is materially damaging business performance$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
